2. Definitions

"Licensor" means edleft (https://github.com/edleft), the copyright holder of the Licensed Material, and
any successor or assign who makes the Licensed Material available under this
License. Wherever this License requires separate written permission or
authorization from the Licensor, it is requested as provided in Section 21.

"Licensee" or "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License.

"Organization" means the legal entity exercising rights under this License, together
with its employees and individual contractors acting solely on its behalf and subject
to confidentiality and use restrictions no less protective than those applicable to
the Organization. A separately incorporated affiliate is a separate Organization
unless the Licensor expressly agrees otherwise in writing.

"CloudBasher Code" means source code, scripts, configuration, test code, examples,
comments, and other software-authored material included in the Licensed Material.

"Documentation" means documentation, explanatory prose, diagrams, examples, and
project-authored reference material included in the Licensed Material.

"Commercial Cybersecurity Use" means use of the Licensed Material in bona fide
cybersecurity research, authorized security testing, defensive security engineering,
security consulting, managed security services, product-security evaluation,
detection engineering, incident response, red-team, blue-team, or purple-team
activities, whether or not performed for compensation.

"Commercialization" means selling, sublicensing for a fee, substantially repackaging
for sale, or making the Licensed Material itself or a substantially derived version
of it a principal commercial product, paid software offering, or externally available
hosted service. Commercialization does not include Commercial Cybersecurity Use merely
because compensation is received for professional services in which the Licensed
Material is used as a tool.

"AI System" means a computational system that uses machine learning, neural networks,
foundation models, large language models, generative models, statistical learning, or
materially similar techniques to infer, generate, classify, predict, transform, or
produce outputs.

"Model" means model weights, parameters, learned representations, adapters, LoRA
weights, checkpoints, fine-tuned checkpoints, or materially similar learned artifacts.

"Internal AI System" means an AI System accessible only to the Organization and its
authorized personnel or contractors, and not distributed, licensed, provided as a
service, or otherwise made available to any person or entity outside that Organization.

"Externally Available AI System" means an AI System, Model, model artifact, API,
hosted service, or AI-enabled product made available, directly or indirectly, to any
person or entity outside the Organization that trained, commissioned, or materially
improved it. This includes public or private customer services, paid or free APIs,
customer-only SaaS, downloadable or open weights, partner distributions, licensed
model artifacts, and publicly released academic or nonprofit models.

"Training" means any process that uses Licensed Material, or material substantially
derived from Licensed Material, to determine, adjust, optimize, or materially improve
Model weights, parameters, learned representations, adapters, checkpoints, or model
behavior. Training includes pre-training, continued pre-training, supervised
fine-tuning, instruction tuning, reinforcement learning, preference optimization,
distillation, and materially similar processes.

"AI Training Dataset" means a dataset intentionally assembled or materially prepared
for Training or material improvement of an AI System.

"Authorized Security Testing" means security testing performed on systems for which
the person conducting the testing has authorization from the system owner or another
party legally empowered to grant that authorization.

