7. Private and Internal AI Use

7.1 Internal AI Training Permitted.
You may use Licensed Material for Training, fine-tuning, adaptation, model evaluation,
embedding generation, semantic indexing, retrieval-augmented generation, and related
AI research if the resulting AI System remains an Internal AI System and all other
terms of this License are satisfied.

7.2 Interactive AI Tools.
You may use an existing AI assistant, coding assistant, or model to analyze, explain,
debug, document, or modify Licensed Material. You may not knowingly submit a
substantial amount of Licensed Material to a third-party AI service when You know
that the service will use that material to Train or materially improve an Externally
Available AI System in a manner prohibited by Section 8.

7.3 Internal RAG and Embeddings.
You may create private or internal search indexes, vector databases, embedding stores,
or retrieval-augmented-generation systems using Licensed Material, provided those
systems and any substantial CloudBasher-derived corpus remain internal to the
Organization except as otherwise expressly permitted by this License.

8. Restrictions on Externally Available AI Systems

8.1 External AI Training Restriction.
Without separate written permission from Licensor, You may not use Licensed Material
to Train or materially improve an AI System if that AI System is, is intended to be,
or later becomes an Externally Available AI System.

8.2 Internal-to-External Transition.
An AI System initially developed as an Internal AI System may not later be made
Externally Available if Licensed Material was used for its Training or material
improvement, unless Licensor separately authorizes that external availability in
writing.

8.3 Training Datasets.
Without separate written permission from Licensor, You may not intentionally include
a substantial amount of Licensed Material in an AI Training Dataset intended for
Training or materially improving an Externally Available AI System, and You may not
publish, sell, license, or externally distribute such a dataset for that purpose.

8.4 Synthetic Circumvention.
You may not intentionally transform, paraphrase, transpile, rewrite, summarize, or
generate synthetic material substantially derived from Licensed Material for the
purpose of circumventing Sections 8.1 through 8.3.

8.5 Evaluation.
You may use Licensed Material to benchmark or evaluate an AI System. If evaluation
results derived from the Licensed Material are then used as a direct training,
optimization, reinforcement, or preference signal that materially improves an
Externally Available AI System, that subsequent activity is subject to Section 8.1.

8.6 No Restriction on Ideas.
Nothing in this Section claims ownership of general ideas, methods, facts,
cybersecurity concepts, or independently developed material that copyright or other
applicable law does not protect.

